WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.116
If you stop

00:00:00.928 --> 00:00:01.965
writing code you

00:00:01.824 --> 00:00:02.944
also get worse

00:00:03.462 --> 00:00:04.688
An essay arguing

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:05.584
that developers who

00:00:05.396 --> 00:00:06.421
hand all coding

00:00:06.233 --> 00:00:07.412
to AI agents

00:00:07.236 --> 00:00:08.403
and only review

00:00:08.214 --> 00:00:09.181
output will see

00:00:08.993 --> 00:00:09.959
their own skills

00:00:10.101 --> 00:00:11.327
including their ability

00:00:11.139 --> 00:00:12.094
to review code

00:00:11.905 --> 00:00:12.424
well

00:00:12.483 --> 00:00:13.615
steadily erode

00:00:14.134 --> 00:00:14.912
The point is

00:00:14.724 --> 00:00:15.702
not the short-term

00:00:15.514 --> 00:00:16.563
quality of agent

00:00:16.375 --> 00:00:16.952
output

00:00:16.988 --> 00:00:18.013
but the long-term

00:00:17.825 --> 00:00:18.591
craft of the

00:00:18.403 --> 00:00:19.110
engineer

00:00:19.158 --> 00:00:20.136
which he argues

00:00:19.948 --> 00:00:21.315
depends on actually

00:00:21.127 --> 00:00:21.940
writing code

00:00:22.478 --> 00:00:24.600
Before 2022 10/10

00:00:24.412 --> 00:00:25.661
engineers would agree

00:00:25.473 --> 00:00:26.381
wholeheartedly

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:27.924
Full story on

00:00:27.735 --> 00:00:28.631
the dashboard
